  "readTime": "10 min read",
  "quickAnswer": "Up to 80% of the allergens, mold spores, pet dander, and bacteria in a typical home are settled on surfaces: mattresses, carpets, upholstery, walls, and inside HVAC ducts. Only a small fraction is airborne at any given moment, and only briefly. This explains why a HEPA air purifier, which can only filter air that passes through it, so often leaves you feeling like the problem never fully went away. Most of the contamination it needs to remove is sitting on the couch, the carpet, and the mattress, where no filter can reach it.",
