    "## First, the reassurance, because you're going to ask",
    "If you found this page, you love your pet and you're not getting rid of them. Nothing in this guide asks you to. Rehoming an animal is heartbreaking, and it's usually not necessary. Plenty of people with real sensitivities live comfortably with cats and dogs by controlling the environment instead of removing the animal.",
    "Pet owners tend to ask about safety first, so: yes, everything recommended here is safe to breathe around your animals. The probiotic approach described below is built on *Bacillus* strains that are FDA GRAS classified, MADE SAFE certified, and EPA registered, with no ozone, no VOCs, and no chemical residue. You are not spraying disinfectant around your dog's bed. If you want the full safety breakdown, [are environmental probiotics safe](/blog/are-environmental-probiotics-safe) covers it in detail.",
    "## What pet dander is (and why it's so persistent)",
