    "- **Your clothes and soft furnishings.** Curtains, cushions, throws.",
    "An air purifier sitting in the corner does nothing for any of these. It cleans the air, and then the dander reservoir reloads the air every time someone sits on the couch or the dog jumps off the bed. So many pet owners say their purifier \"helped a little\" because it did its job on the airborne 20% and never touched the surfaces.",
    "## Why grooming + HEPA isn't the whole answer",
    "Grooming and HEPA are both useful, and you should do both. But each addresses only part of the problem.",
    "**Grooming and bathing** reduce dander at the source, because less shedding means less input. But you can't bathe a cat daily, and even well-groomed pets shed protein constantly. Grooming lowers the input rate without emptying the reservoir already in your furniture.",
    "**HEPA filtration** captures airborne dander efficiently, and for cat allergen, which stays airborne longer, a good HEPA unit in the bedroom helps overnight. But HEPA can only filter air that passes through it. The dander pressed into your carpet pad and sofa cushions never moves through the filter, so the reservoir sits there and keeps refeeding the air. The [best air purifier for allergies](/blog/best-air-purifier-for-allergies) guide breaks down where HEPA wins and where it leaves a gap.",
    "The missing piece is something that treats the surfaces continuously and safely, without chemicals you'd never want to spray near an animal.",
    "## The chemical-free piece: probiotic surface treatment",
    "A probiotic air purifier disperses beneficial *Bacillus* bacteria into the air and onto every surface in the room. Those harmless spores settle into the same carpet, upholstery, and bedding where dander accumulates, and they go to work on the organic debris (the skin flakes, oils, and protein residue) that makes up and surrounds the dander reservoir. By consuming that organic load and colonizing the surface, they reduce the reservoir over time through **competitive exclusion**, the same crowd-out mechanism that keeps a healthy microbiome in balance.",
    "For a pet household, that does four things:",
    "- **Reduces the dander reservoir on soft surfaces**, the part grooming and HEPA can't reach.",
