    "> **Treat the surfaces where dander settles. The Biotica 800 covers up to 800 sq ft and is designed for homes with pets.** [Learn more →](https://shop.envirobiotics.com/products/biotica-800)",
    "## The step-by-step protocol",
    "This routine combines all three layers. Treat it as a weekly rhythm you keep up, since a one-time blitz won't hold.",
    "1. **Groom your pet 2–3× per week, in a low-dander room.** Brushing removes loose dander before it spreads. Do it in a tiled room or outside if you can, not on the carpet you're trying to keep clean.",
    "2. **Bathe regularly: monthly for dogs, as tolerated for cats.** A plain, vet-approved gentle shampoo is enough, because the goal is to rinse off surface allergen and no medication is involved. Don't over-bathe and dry the skin, which increases flaking.",
    "3. **Wash all bedding hot, weekly.** Yours and theirs, at 130°F+ to denature the protein. If your pet sleeps on your bed, your bedding is a pet-bedding too.",
    "4. **HEPA-vacuum soft surfaces weekly.** Cover carpets, rugs, sofas, and pet beds. Go slowly, and use a vacuum that has a sealed HEPA filter so you're not blowing dander back out. Surface-pass vacuuming isn't perfect, but weekly consistency matters more than intensity.",
    "5. **Run a HEPA air purifier where your pet (and you) spend the most time.** The bedroom is the highest-impact placement for overnight relief, especially for cat allergen.",
