    "- **Activated carbon (charcoal) filtration** is the technology that adsorbs many gaseous VOCs and odors. If VOC reduction is your goal and you want a device, look for substantial activated-carbon media and don't rely on a HEPA rating. Carbon saturates over time and needs replacing.",
    "- **Houseplants:** despite the famous NASA study, real-world research shows you'd need an impractical number of plants to lower VOCs by any useful amount in a normal room. Enjoy them, but don't count on them as your VOC strategy.",
