  "quickAnswer": "To test your indoor air quality at home, measure four things: particulate matter (PM2.5), carbon dioxide, humidity, and volatile organic compounds (VOCs). A consumer air quality monitor in the $80–$200 range covers all four and is the single most useful purchase. Add a separate radon test kit, since radon is a distinct health risk no air monitor detects. Keep one limitation in mind: air tests measure what is floating, and most indoor contamination has settled onto surfaces.",
