    "## The four things that work",
    "### 1. Get humidity below 50%: the single highest-leverage change",
    "Because dust mites absorb water from the air, they cannot maintain a population in dry conditions. Sustained relative humidity below roughly 50% is broadly recommended for mite control, and below 40% the environment becomes hostile to them ([EPA](https://www.epa.gov/mold), [AAFA](https://aafa.org/allergies/types-of-allergies/dust-mite-allergy/)).",
    "Practically:",
    "- Buy a **hygrometer** and measure your bedroom. The reading may surprise you.",
