    "- Use **exhaust fans** in bathrooms and kitchens, and run them for 20–30 minutes after use.",
    "- Avoid drying laundry indoors without ventilation, and check that bedroom windows aren't running with condensation overnight.",
    "Do not push below 30%, or you trade a mite problem for dry airways, irritated sinuses, and static. The target band is 40–50%.",
    "### 2. Encase the mattress and pillows",
    "Allergen-proof encasements are tightly woven covers that zip fully around the mattress, pillows, and ideally the duvet. They cut the mites inside off from their food supply, and they put a physical barrier between you and the allergen reservoir that already exists. Allergist guidance recommends encasements more consistently than almost any other intervention, because they address the largest reservoir directly and require no ongoing effort once fitted.",
    "Look for covers specified for allergen or dust mite barrier use with a fully sealed zip. Wash the outer surface periodically along with the rest of the bedding.",
