    "For items that cannot take hot water, freezing works partially. Twenty-four hours in a freezer kills mites in soft toys and small items, but it does not remove the allergen, so you still need to wash the item afterwards to rinse the proteins out. A lot of guides present freezing alone as a complete fix when it does only half the job.",
    "### 4. Reduce and manage soft furnishings",
