  "quickAnswer": "The ideal indoor humidity level is **40–60% relative humidity**, and the practical sweet spot for most homes is 45–50%. Above 60%, you create the conditions mold needs to germinate and dust mites need to reproduce. Below 40%, you get dry airways, irritated sinuses, cracked wood, and static. In winter, aim lower, around 30–40%, to stop condensation forming on cold windows.",
