    "## Why this one number matters more than it sounds",
    "Relative humidity is the percentage of water vapour the air is holding compared with the maximum it could hold at that temperature. It sounds like a comfort setting, but it controls most of the biology in your home.",
    "It governs almost every organism that causes household air complaints. Mold spores are present in all indoor air and stay dormant until a surface is damp enough for them to germinate. Dust mites have no way to drink and absorb moisture directly from the air, so they cannot sustain a population in dry conditions. Bacteria on surfaces need moisture to be metabolically active. Meanwhile your own respiratory tract depends on a moist mucous membrane to trap particles before they reach your lungs.",
