    "6. **Keep air conditioning maintained.** AC dehumidifies as a side effect of cooling, and a poorly maintained system does it badly.",
    "> **Humidity is one lever of five. See the full framework.** [Learn more →](/blog/improve-indoor-air-quality-naturally)",
    "## Too dry: below 40%",
    "Dry air gets far less attention, yet it causes problems every heating season.",
    "**What goes wrong:**",
    "- **Your airways lose their first line of defence.** The mucous membranes lining your nose and throat trap particles and pathogens before they get deeper. Dry air impairs that function, which is part of why dry indoor air in winter is associated with more respiratory irritation.",
    "- **Symptoms mimic allergies.** Dry cough, scratchy throat, congestion, nosebleeds, and itchy eyes can send you looking for allergens that aren't there.",
    "- **Skin and lips crack**, and eczema commonly worsens.",
    "- **Wood shrinks.** Hardwood floors gap, furniture joints loosen, and instruments go out of tune.",
    "- **Static builds up**, which is annoying and occasionally hazardous to electronics.",
    "**Signs you're below the band:** static shocks on carpet, waking with a dry throat, persistent nosebleeds, gapping floorboards, houseplants drying out fast.",
