    "## Seasonal targets",
    "The band shifts in winter for a physical reason: cold surfaces. Warm indoor air holding 50% humidity will condense the moment it touches a single-glazed window at freezing temperature, and mold then grows in that condensation on the frame and sill. In cold weather you run the house drier on purpose.",
    "| Season / condition | Target relative humidity |\n| :---- | :---- |\n| Summer / humid seasons | 45–55% |\n| Winter (mild, above freezing) | 40–45% |\n| Winter (cold, well below freezing) | 30–40% |\n| Nursery / infant room | 40–50% |\n| Homes with confirmed dust mite allergy | 40–45% |",
