      "a": "Match the unit's CADR to your room using the two-thirds rule: required CADR is roughly the room's floor area in square feet multiplied by 0.66, assuming an 8-foot ceiling. A 300 sq ft room needs a CADR of about 200. For allergies or asthma, size up so the CADR roughly equals the room's square footage, which delivers the four to five air changes per hour that allergy guidance recommends."
